extends RefCounted

## The audience as a deal (src/sim/deal.gd, docs/design/v5.3-ab.md section 5). EVERY MONTH
## HERE IS A LABELLED STAND-IN (the parent's ruling, 2026-11-07): the smaller grant has no
## source to read, and no band reads these yet, since the fold into three approaches and its
## lever bands are a later PR. They are the first thing the play gate should move.

## What is asked: a bill brought by a date, a portfolio now, a closing plant saved now, or a
## dated word on the want.
const ASK_LAW := "law"
const ASK_POST := "post"
const ASK_FIRM := "firm"
const ASK_WORD := "word"

## What is offered: a vote on the next bill, or silence.
const OFFER_VOTE := "vote"
const OFFER_SILENCE := "silence"

## The three priced approaches (the spec's fold), the scene's one tension. A win is the smaller
## grant for the same offer. Flatter and friendship fold in as modifiers in a later PR.
const APPROACHES := ["argue", "promise_date", "pressure"]
## The fourth, on the corrupt currencies alone, and only where Deal says the person allows it.
const CORRUPT_APPROACH := "bargain"

## A bill is asked for inside half a year: long enough to book a division.
const LAW_MONTHS := 6
## A word on anything else with no date of its own: a meter, a measure, an office.
const WORD_MONTHS := 12
## The smaller grant: the same word, a year later (a post: the word within a year, not the
## seat now). Bargain's other half, the same offer, is what makes it a smaller grant.
const SMALLER_EXTRA_MONTHS := 12
## How long a person's silence lasts. Silence is real only if a brief reads it, and a brief
## needs a grudge past the gate: a year is about what a refused person takes to get there.
const SILENCE_MONTHS := 12
